"peer_disclosure_id": "intc_2024_1A_D045",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "AMD and Intel both identify natural disasters, climate change, and specifically water availability risks as significant threats to their operations and supply chains. AMD discloses that 'natural disasters, including drought... could disrupt the availability of water necessary for the operations of our business or the business of our suppliers,' while Intel explicitly links climate change to water scarcity, stating it 'could disrupt the availability of water necessary for the operation of our fabrication facilities, including our facilities located in water-sensitive regions such as Arizona and Israel.' Both companies also acknowledge that climate change may increase the frequency or intensity of these disasters.",
