{
"peer_ticker": "MU",
"peer_disclosure_id": "mu_2024_1A_D032",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both AMD and Micron address the risk that climate change and natural disasters will physically disrupt their manufacturing operations and supply chains. AMD notes that 'climate change also may result in chronic changes that result in certain natural disasters occurring more frequently... which could disrupt our operations, or the operations of our third parties.' Micron mirrors this by stating that 'climate change may pose physical risks to our manufacturing facilities or our suppliers' facilities, including increased extreme weather events that could result in supply delays or disruptions.' Both tie the broader concept of climate change directly to operational and supply chain continuity.",
