"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "AMD and Qualcomm both identify natural disasters and the effects of climate change as risks that could disrupt their manufacturing and supply chains in Asia. AMD notes that natural disasters could 'disrupt the ability of our suppliers to deliver expected manufacturing parts,' while Qualcomm is more specific about its geographic exposure, stating that 'If tsunamis, flooding, earthquakes... were to damage, destroy or disrupt any of these facilities... it could disrupt our operations.' Both companies explicitly link climate change effects to these physical disaster risks in their respective supply chain hubs.",
